{:adr/id "2607122400"
 :adr/title "implement the WASM guest ABI's kami:engine/physics apply-impulse host-import"
 :adr/status :accepted
 :adr/date "2026-07-12"
 :adr/related ["2607122200-kami-engine-physics-2d-rigid-body-integration"
               "2607121900-raycast-host-binding"]

 :gap "ADR-2607122200 wired physics-2d into kami.host's ECS via kotoba.physics.contract, but explicitly left a known gap open: the WASM guest ABI's kami:engine/physics@1.0.0 apply-impulse host-import (kotoba.engine-clj.ast :host-import/physics-apply-impulse, declared since ADR-2607121900) was a hardcoded no-op stub in kami.host's import-object. A compiled .kotoba/.cljc guest calling (apply-impulse! eid ix iy iz) linked and ran without erroring, but nothing ever moved -- only the host app (network-isekai's scene EDN) could give an entity a shove via attach-rigid-body!, not gameplay/guest code itself."

 :decision "Add a portable apply-impulse! [state id ix iy] in kami.host (src/kami/host.cljc), placed outside the #?(:cljs ...) block alongside attach-rigid-body!/rigid-body-ids/step-rigid-bodies! so it is directly JVM-testable and compiles identically on :clj/:cljs. It looks up (get-in @state [:rigid-body-2d :bodies id :mass]), and for any id with a live entity and positive mass, applies the standard impulse-momentum relation (Δv = J / m) to :vx/:vy (iz dropped -- physics-2d is XY-plane only). import-object's :apply-impulse now delegates to it in one line: (fn [eid ix iy _iz] (apply-impulse! st (n eid) ix iy)). No-op (silent, no throw) for a missing/despawned entity, an entity with no :physics/body component, or a static body (:mass 0, physics-2d's own never-integrates convention -- also avoids divide-by-zero) -- mirroring the existing guard-and-skip convention :set-position/:set-velocity already use for a missing entity, rather than aborting the guest's whole tick over a harmless no-op shove. This is an external impulse source (gameplay 'give this a shove'), not a new collision-resolution path -- physics-2d.backend's own internal collision response already applies the same Δv=J/m relation each tick inside step-rigid-bodies!; apply-impulse! is a second, independent way to feed a velocity change into the same rigid body. Also fixed a pre-existing, unrelated bug discovered while adding the new test: test/kami/host_rigid_body_test.clj required [physics-2d :as engine] (dash), but physics-2d's own top-level namespace is literally physics_2d (underscore, per its own (ns physics_2d ...) and its own test's [physics_2d :as p]) -- the dash form made Clojure look for a namespace object that doesn't exist, a syntax error that made this entire test file fail to compile, meaning clojure -M:test in kotoba-lang/host was not actually green before this change despite ADR-2607122200's verification section claiming 0 failures. Fixed with the one-character correct require."

 :verification {:host "clojure -M:test: 11 tests / 23 assertions, 0 failures (up from 8/16 -- 3 new tests: exact Δv=J/m through the real production apply-impulse! call path, no-op on no-rigid-body entity, no-op on static body + despawned id). clojure -M:lint: 0 errors, same 3 pre-existing unrelated warnings as before (unused clojure.string/kotoba.physics/kami.gpu requires -- cljs-only-usage false positives, not introduced here)."
                :engine-clj "No code change. Verified via a throwaway, uncommitted REPL check that kotoba.engine-clj's host-import ABI tables (ast.cljc) already had correct, unchanged entries for :host-import/physics-apply-impulse (module-field [kami:engine/physics@1.0.0 apply-impulse], param-kinds [:i64 :f32 :f32 :f32], return-kind :void) since whenever raycast/apply-force were added (ADR-2607121900), and that codegen.cljc's host-import call emission is fully generic/table-driven with no apply-impulse-specific gap. Compiled (defsystem shove [dt] (apply-impulse! 1 (f32 5.0) (f32 10.0) (f32 0.0))) via kotoba.engine-clj/compile-str and confirmed the resulting Module IR's :host-imports contains the exact-correct import declaration. Separately noted: kotoba-lang/engine-clj is GitHub-archived (read-only) as of 2026-07-03; its README claims consolidation into kotoba-lang/kami-engine's kami-engine-clj/ subdirectory, but that subdirectory does not exist on kami-engine's main (404 via GitHub contents API) -- an inconsistency flagged, not resolved, by this ADR."
                :kototama "No code change; read-only grep investigation. Only 'kami:engine' reference in the whole repo is an unrelated negative-test fixture string in test/kototama/contract_test.cljc (wrong-abi-surface-fails-with-data), asserting kototama's own actor:host ABI validator rejects a differently-namespaced ABI surface -- confirms kototama's actor:host ABI and the game engine's kami:engine ABI are deliberately separate systems, not a shared implementation."}

 :consequences ["a compiled .kotoba/.cljc guest can now author a real, physically correct impulse against a rigid-body-2d entity through the WASM ABI -- gameplay code (not just the host app's scene EDN) can make an entity jump, get knocked back, launch a projectile-style shove, etc, closing the gap ADR-2607122200 left open"
                "apply-force (:host-import/physics-apply-force, also declared since ADR-2607121900) remains a no-op -- out of scope here, left for a future ADR if a concrete caller needs continuous force application rather than an instantaneous impulse"
                "kotoba-lang/host's clojure -M:test is now verifiably green end-to-end for the first time -- the pre-existing physics-2d/physics_2d namespace-name test bug is fixed, so ADR-2607122200's prior 0-failures claim (never independently re-verified against a from-scratch deps.edn resolution) is now actually true"
                "the kotoba-lang/engine-clj -> kami-engine/kami-engine-clj migration inconsistency (archived repo says moved, target subdirectory absent upstream) is flagged for whoever owns that migration; not resolved by this ADR"
                "no engine-clj or kototama commits were made -- both investigated and confirmed to need no change"]

